
title:: MITHScreenRatios
summary:: A utility for comparing aspect ratios and calculating rectangle dimensions
related:: Classes/MITHRatiosView
categories:: geometry, gui, scbook

description::
A utility for calculating dimensions and aspect ratios of rectangles, particularly for GUI design. Provides a dictionary of common ratios with musical interval relationships and allows conversion between ratios, cents, and dimensions. Includes methods to find the closest standard ratio to arbitrary dimensions, convert between different representations of musical intervals, and create windows with specific proportions.

classmethods::

method:: new
Returns a new MITHScreenRatios instance.

method:: ratiosDict
Returns a Dictionary of predefined ratios. The dictionary contains named ratios mapped to arrays in the format [[numerator, denominator], "description"].

instancemethods::

private:: init, checkDims, getScreenSize, prProcessScaledRatio, resetDims, resizeWin

subsection:: Dictionary Management

method:: ratiosDict
An instance of the class method of the same name. This instance can be modified with addRatio, addRatioDict, and removeRatio.

method:: addRatioDict
Add or replace multiple entries in the ratio dictionary.
argument:: dict
A Dictionary with entries in the format key -> [[num, denom], "description"]
argument:: replace
Boolean, if true replaces the entire dictionary, if false (default) merges with existing dictionary

method:: addRatio
Add a single custom ratio to the ratios dictionary.
argument:: key
Symbol or String name for the new ratio
argument:: ratioArr
Array [numerator, denominator]
argument:: description
Optional description string

method:: removeRatio
Remove a ratio from the dictionary.
argument:: key
Symbol or String name of the ratio to remove

method:: ratioObject
Returns an Association for a named ratio.
argument:: key
Symbol or String name of the ratio
returns:: Association

subsection:: Ratio Operations

method:: getRatio
Gets a ratio array from the dictionary by name.
argument:: ratioName
Symbol or String name of the ratio
returns:: Array [numerator, denominator]

method:: reduceRatio
Reduces a ratio to its simplest form. Can handle floating-point inputs.
argument:: ratioArray
Array [numerator, denominator]
returns:: Array [numerator, denominator] in simplified form

method:: ratio
Convenience polymorphic method that either gets a named ratio from the dictionary (using method getRatio) or reduces an array to its simplest ratio form (using reduceRatio).
argument:: input
A Symbol, String, or Array [num, denom]
returns:: Array [numerator, denominator]


method:: ratioToDecimal
Converts a ratio to its decimal representation.
argument:: arr
Array [numerator, denominator]
argument:: precision
Integer specifying decimal places (default: 4)
returns:: Float

method:: asRatio
Converts a decimal value to the closest ratio with denominator <= maxDenominator.
argument:: decimal
Float value to convert
argument:: maxDenominator
Maximum denominator to use in approximation (default: 100)
returns:: Array [numerator, denominator]

method:: ratioToCents
Converts a ratio to cents (musical interval measurement).
argument:: ratio
Symbol, String, or Array [numerator, denominator]
returns:: Integer number of cents

method:: centsToRatio
Converts cents to the closest simple ratio.
argument:: cents
Number of cents
argument:: maxDenominator
Maximum denominator to use in approximation (default: 100)
returns:: Array [numerator, denominator]

method:: diffInCents
Calculates the difference in cents between two ratios.
argument:: arr1
First ratio (Symbol, String, or Array)
argument:: arr2
Second ratio (Symbol, String, or Array)
argument:: precision
Decimal precision for the result (default: 2)
returns:: Float difference in cents

method:: ratioDescr
Returns the description for a named ratio.
argument:: name
Symbol or String name of the ratio
returns:: String description or nil

subsection:: Search and Analysis

method:: searchRatios
Search for ratios by name, value, or description.
argument:: searchTerm
Symbol, String, or Number to search for
argument:: printResults
Boolean, if true (default) prints results to post window
returns:: Dictionary of matching ratios

method:: closestRatio
Find the predefined ratio that most closely matches given dimensions.
argument:: ratio
Array [width, height]
argument:: precision
Decimal precision for comparison (default: 4)
argument:: highPrecision
Boolean, if true uses exact calculations (default: false)
returns:: Association with the closest matching ratio

method:: ratioObjectData
Returns complete data for a ratio as an array.
argument:: ratioObject
Association from ratioObject or ratioDict.associationAt
argument:: precision
Decimal precision (default: 4)
returns:: Array [key, ratio, description, decimal, cents]

subsection:: Display Methods

method:: sortRatios
Sort ratios by their decimal value or other criteria.
argument:: array
Optional array of ratios to sort (default: all ratios)
argument:: sortIndex
Index to sort by (e.g. 0=key, 4=cents) (default: 3)
argument:: precision
Decimal precision (default: 4)
returns:: Sorted array of ratio data

method:: postRatioArr
Prints a formatted ratio array to the post window.
argument:: ratioArr
Array in the format [key, ratio, description, decimal, cents]

method:: listRatios
Lists all or specified ratios with their values and descriptions.
argument:: array
Optional array of ratios to list (default: all ratios)

method:: postRatio
Posts details of a specific ratio by name.
argument:: name
Symbol or String name of the ratio
returns:: Association or this

subsection:: GUI / Screen Methods

method:: gui
Creates a new MITHRatiosView with this MITHScreenRatios instance.
argument:: window
Optional existing window to use (default: creates new window)
returns:: MITHRatiosView

method:: win
Returns the gui Window, if it exists

method:: screenDims
Get or set the current screen dimensions.
returns:: Array [width, height]

method:: maxDims
Get or set the maximum allowed dimensions.
argument:: arr
Array [width, height] or Number
returns:: Array [width, height]

method:: viewDims
Get or set the current view dimensions.
argument:: arr
Array [width, height] or Number
returns:: Array [width, height] or this

method:: ratioToDims
Calculate dimensions based on a ratio, constrained to maximum dimensions.
argument:: ratio
Symbol, String, or Array [numerator, denominator]
argument:: dims
Optional constraint dimensions (default: maxDims)
argument:: landscape
Boolean, if true (default) width > height, if false height > width
returns:: Array [width, height]

method:: close
Close gui Window if it exists


examples::

code::
// create a new instance
m = MITHScreenRatios.new;

// list all available ratios
m.listRatios;

// search for ratios containing "third" in their description
m.searchRatios("third");

// calculate dimensions for a 16:9 ratio with width 800
m.ratioToDims(\r16_9, 800);  // [800, 450]

// find the closest standard ratio to arbitrary dimensions
m.closestRatio([683, 384]);  // (r16_9 -> [[9, 16], minor 7th])

// create a window with phi (golden) ratio
d = m.ratioToDims(\phi, 800) // [800, 494]
m.viewDims_(d); // set default dims to [800, 494]
m.viewDims // [800, 494]
m.gui; // create a view Window with viewDims dimensions

m.viewDims_([640, 480]) // gui Window updates its size
m.viewDims // [640, 480]
m.close // close window

// convert a ratio to cents
r = m.ratio(\r3_2) // [3, 2]
m.ratioToCents(r);  // 702

//  calculate difference between just and equal-tempered major third
m.diffInCents(\r5_4, m.centsToRatio(400));  // 13.79

// add a custom ratio
m.addRatio("myRatio", [11, 8], "undecimal neutral fourth");
m.postRatio("myRatio");

// find all ratios in the dictionary that use specific numbers
m.searchRatios(5);  // Finds ratios containing the number 5

// example: search for specific ratios and replace dictionary
(
m = MITHScreenRatios.new;
// search for all semitone ratios
~semitoneRatios = m.searchRatios("semitone", false);
// replace entire dictionary with just these results
m.addRatioDict(~semitoneRatios, true);
// verify only semitone ratios are in Dictionary
m.listRatios;
)
/*
// returns
\r25_24 : [25, 24] "just intonation major semitone" 0.96 | 71 cents
\r18_17 : [18, 17] "equal temperament semitone" 0.9444 | 99 cents
\r16_15 : [16, 15] "just intonation minor semitone" 0.9375 | 112 cents
*/

// Convert 700 cents to ratio
m.centsToRatio(700); // [442, 295]

// example: create golden ratio window
(
m = MITHScreenRatios.new;
// get phi (golden ratio) dimensions with 600px width
d = m.ratioToDims(\phi, 600);
m.viewDims_(d);
// create window and display dimensions
m.gui;
("Golden ratio window: % x %").format(d[0], d[1]).postln;
)
// flip aspect ration, defaults to full screen height
m.viewDims_(m.ratioToDims(\phi, landscape: false));



// EExample: Find musical ratios within a specific range
(
m = MITHScreenRatios.new;
// search for ratios between 600-700 cents (around a tritone)
~tritoneRatios = Dictionary.new;
m.ratiosDict.keysValuesDo({ |key, value|
    ~cents = m.ratioToCents(value[0]);
    if(~cents.inclusivelyBetween(580, 620)) {
        ~tritoneRatios.put(key, value);
    };
});
// add to dictionary
m.addRatioDict(~tritoneRatios, true);
m.listRatios;
)
::